#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -Eeuo pipefail
###############################################################################
# Script: setup
# Company: Solutionz INC / RSW
# Revision: V06.100626N
# Created by Reiko Seneathia Williams
# Release Date: 2026-10-06
# Dual-Homed WAN/LAN + Auto-Validation Update: 2026-10-18
# Security Hardening Update: 2026-11-03
# Live Network Discovery Update: 2026-11-03
# Integrated Domotz Activation Update: 2026-11-04
# Optional LAN / UFW sysctl persistence / network-validator NTP update: 2026-11-04
# Default engineering account / login-policy update: 2026-11-04
# Post-reboot unified menu + engineering credential provisioning update: 2026-11-05
# Engineering-key protected credential provisioning update: 2026-11-05
# Production engineering-key preflight/fingerprint validation update: 2026-11-05
#
# Purpose:
#   Build and harden the Solutionz RMM Agent on the approved Protectli V1210
#   Ubuntu 24.04 LTS operating-system family, record the manufacturer-delivered
#   package state, install/validate required components, install Domotz, configure
#   the V1210 USB-C COM serial console, and automatically generate and validate a
#   dual-homed network design in which eth0 is the WAN/cloud interface and eth1 is
#   the AV/control LAN interface. The script supports DHCP or true static WAN,
#   DHCP/static/native LAN addressing, 802.1Q VLANs on eth1, automatic post-change
#   validation, and rollback when a network change is locally invalid.
#
# Important:
#   - General "apt upgrade -y" is intentionally NOT used.
#   - Domotz is intentionally not revision-pinned. The installed Snap revision
#     is recorded for audit, and updates are governed by operating policy.
#   - The V1210 USB-C port labeled COM is a serial console, not USB Ethernet.
#     This script exposes an authenticated login on ttyS0 and automatically
#     launches the Solutionz local configuration menu for restricted technician
#     accounts on interactive SSH, local console, or USB-C COM login. Authenticated
#     engineering logins also land on the same menu in ENGINEERING mode, where an
#     engineering shell is available only after engineering authentication.
#   - The default engineering login is solz_eng. Setup creates/configures the
#     account but never embeds a password. A Solutionz engineering SSH public key
#     is installed for first access. After Phase 2 validates successfully, an
#     engineer authenticates as solz_eng with the matching private key, enters the
#     same Solutionz menu in ENGINEERING mode, and selects option 9 to create the
#     local solz_eng password. Technicians cannot perform this first-time setup.
#   - Only the public SSH key is stored in Setup/on the appliance. The matching
#     private key remains with Solutionz Engineering and is never copied to GitHub
#     or to a V1210 appliance.
#   - Technicians cannot create, change, or provision the solz_eng password.
#   - Ubuntu 24.04 LTS is the controlled OS family. Supported Noble point
#     releases include Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS.
#   - Network changes are staged and take effect after manual reboot unless the
#     onsite network utility explicitly applies a validated change.
#   - Netplan/VLAN configuration can be generated automatically from a JSON
#     network profile. VLAN IDs are never guessed from a switch trunk; they must
#     be supplied in the profile or guided wizard.
#   - eth0 is the WAN/cloud interface. It may use DHCP (including MAC-reserved or
#     port-policy DHCP) or a true static IPv4 configuration and is the only
#     interface permitted to own the IPv4 default route and system DNS.
#   - eth1 is the AV/control LAN interface. It may use untagged DHCP/static IPv4,
#     act as an unnumbered 802.1Q trunk parent, or carry both native and tagged LAN
#     networks. eth1 and all VLANs linked to eth1 are prohibited from installing
#     a default route or DHCP-provided DNS.
#   - The RMM Agent is not a WAN-to-LAN router. IPv4 forwarding is explicitly
#     disabled and validated. Local Domotz/RMM processes can communicate through
#     both interfaces, but traffic is not forwarded between them.
#   - After every onsite network change the same installed network validator runs
#     automatically. Locally invalid addressing/VLAN/default-route changes are
#     rolled back. Upstream DNS/cloud-connectivity failures are reported without
#     discarding an otherwise valid customer-provided addressing configuration.
#   - USB-C COM remains the independent recovery/configuration path when either
#     Ethernet interface is unavailable or being reconfigured.
#   - Security hardening enforces UFW deny-incoming/deny-routed defaults while
#     preserving Domotz-required inbound TCP 22 and TCP 3000; disables IP
#     forwarding, redirects, source routing and proxy ARP; hardens SSH; enables
#     auditd/AppArmor; restricts the field-tech path; and maintains a SHA-256
#     integrity baseline that is revalidated around approved network changes.
#   - Live network discovery reads the running kernel/network state before the
#     technician is asked to configure anything. It reports MAC, carrier, link
#     state, negotiated speed, active IPv4, DHCP-vs-manual indication, gateway,
#     default route, DNS and live VLAN state without treating Netplan as observed
#     state. Netplan remains the persistent configuration mechanism across reboot.
#     A true static address that has never been configured or delivered by DHCP
#     cannot be inferred safely and is therefore never guessed.
#   - Secure Boot, TPM-backed disk encryption, CIS remediation, SIEM/EDR and
#     custom AppArmor application profiles are not auto-enabled by this build.
#     They remain Phase-2 controls requiring V1210/Domotz compatibility testing.
#   - NTP synchronization is standardized on systemd-timesyncd. Phase 2 is not
#     gated by time-sync.target; validators perform a bounded 180-second current-boot
#     synchronization check so NTP failure is reported instead of blocking validation.
#   - Serial-console acceptance is based on ttyS0 presence, serial-getty systemd
#     enabled/active state, and GRUB configuration; a transient agetty process
#     match is diagnostic only and is not a production failure criterion.
###############################################################################

